at is open with Tina Smith retiring, and Democrats have nominated Lieutenant Governor Peggy Flanagan against Republican Michele Tafoya, a former sportscaster. The state leans Democratic by a modest three points, and Flanagan has raised more money, though outside groups have spent heavily against her.\n\nRecent polls show a surprisingly tight race, with several surveys putting the candidates within a point or two and one Republican-sponsored poll showing a narrow Democratic lead. Despite that, nearly every expert rating calls the race Likely Democratic, and prediction markets price Flanagan's chances near 90 percent. The forecast lands on a modest Democratic edge with elevated uncertainty, reflecting the gap between the polls and the broader fundamentals.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.8725, "margin": 5.75}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7776, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8131, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8217, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7867, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.784, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7719, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7956, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7935, "margin": 4.5}]}